module test.claim.fleet_naming_witness

// WHAT IS CLAIMED, IN ONE LINE. The five rows the P2 lottery added to the production roster are what the
// allocator itself yields (not hand-picked), the naming policy issues exactly the labels the roster
// records, and the naming/endpoint model refuses what it is supposed to refuse. The claim exists because
// the alternative is a comment in gunbc/hostname_allocation.dag asserting that the recorded names are
// drawn -- an assertion nothing checks.
//
// WHY THE RE-DRAW IS AGAINST THE PRODUCTION ROSTER AND NOT A FIXTURE. A fixture proves the allocator works;
// only the production roster proves THESE rows came from it. The prior list for a row is every row the
// roster holds besides that one, because that is the state the draw was made against -- re-drawing against
// a different prior set would be checking a different lottery.
//
// THE CLAIM RUNS AS A CLAIM: `gunbc run --claim-run --entry dag/test/claim/fleet_naming_witness.dag`,
// where every `test fn` here executes over one load of one closure.

